MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cloud Mail SUPER RSS READER: fetch <base>/channels.json from the rss-gateway and
provision every channel as a nested folder tree (Cloud-Infra/CICD/GH, Cloud-Infra/
Logs/<vm>/<container>, Cloud-Apps/<cat>/<svc>, …), organised exactly like email
folders.

- CommsAccounts.ensureFeedTree/ensureGroupFolder/ensureLeafFolder/pruneFeedTree:
  folder.name = full path (satisfies the (account,name) unique index, avoids
  leaf-label collisions), folder.display = title; group nodes selectable=false;
  leaf identity = feed URL so renames/moves keep messages + read state; removed
  channels pruned scoped by gateway origin (never touches manual feeds / the
  releases seed). Repairs done as a single updateFolder write.
- WorkerFeedSync.sync(): provisions the tree each run when comms_cloud_channels is
  set (offline-tolerant) + per-run failed-host skip set (a dead gateway must not
  cost ~150×20s timeouts under WorkManager's ~10-min cap).
- FragmentDialogCloudFeeds: 'Subscribe to the whole channel tree' checkbox →
  ensureFeedTree + WorkerFeedSync.oneShot (fills immediately, no 6h wait).
- channels.json contract served by cloud 2_configs build-ntfy-rss-channels.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
